### Please describe the problem in your own words.
git-annex fails to build with -f-memory because git-annex uses memory even when crypton does not.

### What steps will reproduce the problem?
Build `git-annex` using -f-memory.

### What version of git-annex are you using? On what operating system?
* OS: Arch Linux
* Kernel: Linux 7.2.14-arch1-1
* GHC: 9.6.7
* git-annex: 10.20261026
* crypton: 1.1.0
* ram: 0.22.1
* memory: 0.18.0

### Please provide any additional information below.

Two files explicitly import from memory. They are used internally by git-annex and are acknowledged in cac57ad1fef58a4d50fcc9818b5e86edaf1a7cd2.

The introduction of the Memory flag in 51de0b3a617a77c6fe8a5f4b5c9b531eabd42bb0 removes the memory dependency when using crypton 1.1.0. This leads to the observed build failure.

The obvious fix would be to add memory as a dependency even with -f-memory; the resulting inconsistency might require a renaming of the flag.

[[!format sh """
[ 38 of 763] Compiling Utility.Hash.Types ( Utility/Hash/Types.hs, dist/build/git-annex/git-annex-tmp/Utility/Hash/Types.dyn_o )

Utility/Hash/Types.hs:14:1: error:
    Could not find module ‘Data.ByteArray.Encoding’
    Perhaps you meant
      Data.ByteArray.Encoding (needs flag -package-id memory-0.18.0)
      Data.ByteArray.Encoding (from ram-0.22.1)
      Data.ByteArray.Mapping (needs flag -package-id memory-0.18.0)
   |
14 | import qualified "memory" Data.ByteArray.Encoding as BAE
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
[...]
[ 83 of 763] Compiling Utility.IPAddress ( Utility/IPAddress.hs, dist/build/git-annex/git-annex-tmp/Utility/IPAddress.dyn_o )

Utility/IPAddress.hs:25:1: error:
    Could not find module ‘Data.Memory.Endian’
    Perhaps you meant
      Data.Memory.Endian (needs flag -package-id memory-0.18.0)
      Data.Memory.Endian (from ram-0.22.1)
   |
25 | import "memory" Data.Memory.Endian
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

# End of transcript or log.
"""]]

### Have you had any luck using git-annex before? (Sometimes we get tired of reading bug reports all day and a lil' positive end note does wonders)


